<!-- FOUNDER / OUR STORY -->
<section class="founder" id="about">
  <div class="section-inner">

    <!-- Full-width lead paragraph -->
    <div class="founder-lead-wrap reveal">
      <div class="section-tag founder-lead-tag"><div class="line"></div><span>The Founding</span></div>
      <h2 class="founder-lead-headline">Built from<br>the <span class="accent">Ground Up</span></h2>
      <p class="founder-lead-p">In 1987, K. R. Subramanian established Jayveecons, Consultants and Engineers in Bengaluru as a process engineering consultancy committed to enhancing efficiency, reliability, and process performance in small-scale cement plants, with deep expertise in Vertical Shaft Kiln technology. What began as a specialized advisory practice quickly evolved into something far more significant—driven by the growing need for practical, reliable, and performance-oriented engineering solutions.</p>
      <div class="founder-lead-divider"></div>
      <p class="founder-lead-sub">The strength of those early engagements—and the trust earned through them—expanded our footprint across industries including mining, food processing, steel, and waste management. As client requirements became more complex and execution-driven, it became clear that consultancy alone would not deliver comprehensive solutions to our customer's needs. This was our natural catalyst to build.</p>
    </div>

    <!-- Two-column body -->
    <div class="founder-body">
      <div class="founder-copy reveal">
        <p>Jayveecons transitioned into a fully integrated design and manufacturing organization—investing in infrastructure, capability, and people. Today, we operate a <strong>90,000 sq.ft machining and fabrication facility</strong>, delivering end-to-end material handling and process equipment solutions under one roof.</p>
        <div class="founder-quote">
          <p>“At Jayveecons, Moving your world ahead is not a statement—it is a responsibility. Our role is to deliver engineering solutions that are not only cost-effective, but fundamentally reliable, efficient, and continuously improving through technology.”</p>
          <cite>— Jayveecons Company Mission</cite>
        </div>
        <p>Over the past three decades, our greatest asset has been the feedback and trust of our customers. Every machine we design carries with it the lessons of real-world operation—refined through performance, iteration, and accountability in the field. This continuous feedback loop has shaped our engineering philosophy and remains the foundation of our growth.</p>
        <p>Today, that experience is embedded into how we design the future. Through platforms like VECTRIX™, we are formalizing decades of practical knowledge into predictive engineering systems—enabling faster innovation, greater accuracy, and smarter equipment design.</p>
        <p>As we look ahead, our focus remains clear: to build the next generation of industrial equipment under the VECTOMEC™ line—systems that reflect not just where the industry is today, but where it needs to go. Our commitment is to continue evolving with our customers, delivering solutions that move their operations—and the industries we serve—forward with confidence.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="reveal">
        <!-- Engineering delivery process cards — non-repetitive from homepage -->
        <div class="process-cards">
          <div class="proc-card">
            <div class="proc-num">01</div>
            <div class="proc-content">
              <div class="proc-title">Concept &amp; Engineering Design</div>
              <div class="proc-desc">Every project starts with your process requirements. Our engineers design to your capacity, material, and site parameters — not to a generic catalogue spec.</div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="proc-card">
            <div class="proc-num">02</div>
            <div class="proc-content">
              <div class="proc-title">In-House Fabrication</div>
              <div class="proc-desc">90,000 sq.ft of machining and fabrication capability. We manufacture to our own drawings, under our own quality control. Nothing critical is subcontracted.</div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="proc-card">
            <div class="proc-num">03</div>
            <div class="proc-content">
              <div class="proc-title">Erection &amp; Commissioning</div>
              <div class="proc-desc">Our teams install and commission at your site — ensuring the equipment that leaves our floor arrives performing to specification in the field.</div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="proc-card">
            <div class="proc-num">04</div>
